  "term": "reinforcement therapy",
  "definition": "Reinforcement therapy, in this source, refers to Circadian Reinforcement Therapy: a proposed intervention that creates a structured daily routine by regularly timing cues such as light exposure, exercise, meals, and social contact to help stabilize the sleep–wake cycle.",
